# HP ROSCon Policy Evaluation Dashboard

## Purpose
Read-only dashboard proving the flywheel claim: a policy trained on more curated episodes has a measurably higher success rate. Measurement layer for the SO-ARM booth demo and policy promotion decisions.

## Demo story (Conv 1)
- SO-ARM sim runs ACT policy placing 3 cubes on a tray
- Green cube randomly shifted 3cm — adapting to random placement is the new behavior
- Baseline: known-good policy trained on 5 success episodes vs versions trained on 10/20/40 successes
- Expect: fewer failures and smoother successes as training set grows

## Data sources (read-only)
| Mode | Config | Reads |
|------|--------|-------|
| `files` | `SOURCE_MODE=files`, `RECORDS_DIR` | Directory of episode JSON (booth/offline) |
| `live` | `SOURCE_MODE=live`, `.env.local` | Kafka `episode-manifests` + MinIO `episodes-curated` + `episodes-rejected` |

Live endpoints (Tailscale required): MinIO `http://10.0.0.49:30900`, Kafka `10.0.0.49:30903`

## Critical data rules
- **Success rate** = `task_success==true` / all eligible episodes. Must include **rejected** episodes — curated-only is ~100% by construction.
- **has_failure** episodes: exclude (injected demo failures, not real outcomes)
- **eval-*** model_versions: drop client-side (Kafka history still has them; MinIO was scrubbed)
- **pre-teacher**: group `soarm-act-10ep-10k` and `soarm-act-v1` (legacy Phase-2 tags)
- **Smoothness**: successes only (failures barely move → would make weak policy look smoother)
- **dataset_path**: ignore, don't break on it
- Group by `model_version` as-is; don't fix mislabeled history

## Version mapping (`config/versions.yaml`, gitignored)
```yaml
upstream-act-teacher: 0    # baseline / teacher-as-shipped
act-v2-ft160: 160          # fine-tuned on 160 curated successes
```
Leave fixture versions unmapped. Optional richer ladder: `docs/eval-records/phase3-ladder/*.json` in hp-roscon-flywheel repo (0→73%, 20→60%, 40→56%, 80→76%, 160→86%).

## Run commands
```bash
./run.sh files   # offline, default RECORDS_DIR=tests/fixtures
./run.sh live    # needs .env.local with S3_ACCESS_KEY/S3_SECRET_KEY (olga-readonly)
```

## Guardrails
- Read-only — no writes to Kafka, MinIO, or sim
- Runs on developer machine, not demo desktop
- No pipeline code changes (episode_emitter, curator, sync-agent)
- No persisted state — replay from source reproduces same numbers

